    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0444" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee/704: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-12-15T13:00:00-05:00">December 15,
                            1933—1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>313. Your 335, December 15, 11 a.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d259-f1"/> Dodd has
                    telegraphed summary of original Hitler proposals and Lindsay, in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> dated December 8,<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d259-f2"/> has furnished us with British reply requesting further
                    clarification.</p>
                <p>Cable brief summary of subsequent correspondence, together with your analysis of
                    British Government’s present policy and objectives.</p>
                <p>Mail cipher text to Berlin and Geneva.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
